agraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use an index when you often look entities up by a component’s value, such as finding an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity by its name:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let bob = world.spawn(Name(value: \"bob\"), Health(current: 3))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"ada\"), Health(current: 4))","world.index(Name.self)","","print(world.lookup(Name(value: \"bob\")) == [bob])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Spawning, inserting, removing and despawning keep the index current. A change made in place,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the world’s subscript, an update or a mutable span, leaves the index out of date","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until the next ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/advanceChangeTick()","type":"reference"},{"text":", which a schedule calls before each system, rebuilds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. Until then, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lookup(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" walks the storage, so its answer is always current. Index a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type whose values change rarely. Indexing a type twice keeps one index. A copy of the world","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its indexes; a snapshot doesn’t.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" entities holding a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"kind":"co